# Standards Compliance Waivers
#
# Waive specific controls by framework. Waived controls count as
# "accepted" in compliance scoring — visible on dashboards, not hidden.
# Waivers inherit down the directory tree, just like common.vgo.
#
# Place this file at any directory level:
#   - Root level: waivers apply fleet-wide
#   - Subdirectory: waivers apply only to envoys in that subtree
#
# Framework keys match the compliance tags used in module definitions
# (e.g., cis-ubuntu, pci-dss, hipaa, nist-800-53, soc2, iso-27001).
#
# Fields:
#   control:     Control ID (must match the ID in the compliance tag)
#   reason:      Justification for the waiver (required)
#   approved_by: Who approved the waiver (required)
#   expires:     Optional expiration date (YYYY-MM-DD). Expired waivers
#                are automatically excluded from scoring.
#
# Uncomment any control below to waive it. Every control is commented
# out by default — nothing is waived until you explicitly enable it.

waivers:

